In article <1454@sirius.ucs.adelaide.edu.au> ganderse@adelphi.ua.oz.au.oz.au (Geoff Andersen) writes:
>   Which one is better? Are they the same? I have resistance to fire, sleep
>   shock, cold, poison and (I think) disintegration. I have been told that only
>   gray dragon scale mail provides magic resistance, is this true?

A cloak of magic resistance will also provide magic resistance.  These are
the only two objects which will.  As far as what type of dragon scale mail you
want, most people go with gray, so that they can use a cloak of displacement,
which will virtually guarantee that you get missed the first time a monster
attacks you.

>Also do the items in the polypile change their curse/blessedness. eg if I have a
>+5 longsword will it polymorph into, say, a +5 katana, or will it be +0 or some
>random variation. Similarly, will an item remain cursed under polymorph?

Polymorphing an object totally changes it.  The only thing which is absolutely
sure to remain the same is what general type of object it is (i.e. scroll,
potion, weapon, armor, etc.).  For instance, if you polymorphed an uncursed
longsword +1, you could end up with:
     a blessed broadsword +3
     a cursed dagger -2
     an uncursed dart
Obviously, many other variations exist.

>Jabberwocks were not mentioned in the spoiler sheet (the only one I didn't know)
>and a friend of mine says they don't give any intrinsics. I am too chicken to
>try at the moment, as this is my best game, so can anyone tell me what effects
>come from eating one?

No intrinsics, 60 food value, 600 weight.

>Lastly, I have a bag of holding. Should I bless it? I didn't quite understand
>the spoiler sheet on this part. I will almost certainly be going after the Wiz,
>and since he curses items, should I bless it for that reason?

I'll check this out, since I'm partly responsible for the sheets.  I believe
that Ken threw that in there though.  Here's the deal with bags of holding:
There is a bug associated with the bag of holding which modifies the weight
of the bag if you bless or curse it.  Basically, if you bless the bag, it 
can end up becoming heavier, and if you curse it, it can actually become
lighter.  This depends on what you have in the bag when you bless/curse it,
and whether or not you take them out afterwards, etc.  I'm not completely
sure on the details.  Now, this bug may have been fixed, but I'm not
totally sure.  Ken Arromdee?  Any comments?

